      "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/folio-assistant-core/process/Process_BoardPlaceNote",
      "@type": "https://litlfred.github.io/bootstrap/v0/ns#Process",
      "name": "Board: place a note",
      "summary": "Putting a note at a spot on a board: write the note into the folio, record where it was drawn on THIS board, and sweep any position whose note has gone.",
      "description": "Putting a note at a spot on a board: write the note into the folio, record where it was drawn on THIS board, and sweep any position whose note has gone.\n\nYou are in this process whenever a note is to appear somewhere. The first gateway exists because the note may already be there — placing is not the same as creating, and a process that conflated them would duplicate content every time somebody moved something.\n\nThe rule the diagram holds is in the first activity's own wording: the note goes into the folio WITH NO COORDINATE. A folio is complete with no board, so a coordinate on a note would make the content depend on a drawing of it. The x,y belongs to the layer, keyed to one board, and an orphaned position is swept from the LAYER rather than being allowed to keep a note alive.",
      "enforcement": "advisory",
      "sourcePath": "processes/ui/board-place-note.bpmn",
      "sourceUrl": "https://github.com/litlfred/folio-assistant-core/blob/main/processes/ui/board-place-note.bpmn",
